message: "If you use this software in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Galerkin Finite Elements in Python: Poisson and Heat Equation on the Unit Square"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-10
license: MIT
authors:
  - given-names: "Mintesinot Alemayehu"
    family-names: "Akale"
    affiliation: "Bahir Dar Institute of Technology, Bahir Dar University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mintesinot-A/fem-poisson-heat"
abstract: >-
  A small, readable finite element code (NumPy/SciPy only) with P1 and P2
  triangular elements, written to verify the method against manufactured
  smooth solutions and to examine numerically how convergence rates depend
  on the regularity of the solution.
keywords:
  - finite element method
  - Galerkin
  - Poisson equation
  - heat equation
  - convergence analysis
  - Python
